  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Booz Allen Hamilton has $4.6B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 851 awards, with an average award size of $5.3M. Obligations are down 31.0% year over year. The General Services Administration and the Department of Defense are the largest federal buyers, accounting for $1.9B and $1.5B of obligations respectively. Engineering Services and Computer Systems Design Services are the top NAICS markets, with $1.3B and $1.2B in obligations respectively. Historical obligations peaked in FY24 at $7.1B and then fell to $6.6B in FY25 before reaching $4.6B in FY26 to date. The dataset covers contract obligations; award-value totals in certain tables are total contract values rather than obligations. Readers should treat FY2026 totals as partial, fiscal year to date figures. This snapshot highlights where federal spending is concentrated by agency and by market, and shows a year-over-year decline in obligations while maintaining a substantial program footprint across civilian and defense customers.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Booz Allen Hamilton's top federal buyers?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the top buyer with $1.9B in obligations. The Department of Defense follows with $1.5B in obligations. Other notable buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $282M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $275M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and markets dominate Booz Allen Hamilton's federal work?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market with $1.3B in obligations, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $1.2B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounts for $615M, and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounts for $532M. Custom Computer Programming Services represents $381M of obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Booz Allen Hamilton make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Booz Allen Hamilton has $4.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 851 awards so far in FY2026 to date and the average award size is $5.3M. Obligations are down 31.0% year over year compared with prior fiscal periods."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Booz Allen Hamilton?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration and the Department of Defense are the largest buyers of Booz Allen Hamilton in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $1.9B and the Department of Defense obligated $1.5B. Other buying agencies include the Department of Health and Human Services at $282M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $275M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Booz Allen Hamilton sell to the government?",
      "a": "Booz Allen Hamilton sells professional and technical services to the government, led by Engineering Services and Computer Systems Design Services. Engineering Services has $1.3B in obligations and Computer Systems Design Services has $1.2B in obligations. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounts for $615M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounts for $532M."
    },
